# Project architecture

ASP.NET Core **.NET 10** API + **Angular 22** SPA (`academy.client`), Clean Architecture.

## Layers (dependencies flow inward)

| Project | Role |
|---------|------|
| `Academy.Domain` | Entities, enums, value objects — no infra deps |
| `Academy.Application` | MediatR features, DTOs, contracts, FluentValidation |
| `Academy.Persistence` | EF Core + SQL Server, migrations, seed |
| `Academy.Infrastructure` | Identity, JWT, DI registration |
| `Academy.Server` | Controllers, hubs, middleware, SPA host |
| `academy.client` | Angular UI; uses NSwag-generated API client |

## Hard rules

- Controllers stay thin: authorize → map request → `ISender.Send` → `result.ToActionResult()`.
- Business logic lives in Application handlers, not controllers or Angular.
- Do not reference Persistence/Infrastructure types from Domain.
- Prefer existing patterns (Result, roles, feature folders) over new abstractions.
- After API contract changes, rebuild Server so NSwag regenerates `academy-api.generated.ts`.
